Streaming tool execution for DSH 0.2.2-rc.1

This package originated from @teddybear/dsh-streaming-tool-execution 0.2.0-rc.2
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Te-ddybear), a plugin port of
"feat(agent-loop): execute parallel-safe tool calls while streaming":
Te-ddybear/deepseek-harness@de079108d2dcbef687ab6457b2bb7987fb67d292

The package retains the name mindagent-dsh-streaming-tool-execution.
The earlier MindAgent adaptation removed bare host imports and used the
0.2.0-rc.2 scheduler symbol. This branch replaces that integration for
0.2.2-rc.1 with ToolsService admission/batch interception and the selected
NativeToolExecutor pipeline. It preserves ordered policy and native completion,
blocks speculative execution at exclusive calls, and drains abandoned work.
Non-native executors retain their normal behavior.

The runtime module still imports no host package and reads its boolean config
directly. Tests use exact published DSH development packages. Package metadata,
localized documentation and installation checks describe the new host contract.

